<p><strong>Summary</strong>: in this tutorial, you will learn how to create a PostgreSQL <code>AFTER INSERT</code> trigger to call a function automatically after a row is inserted into a table.</p>
<h2 id="introduction-to-the-postgresql-after-insert-trigger" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Introduction to the PostgreSQL AFTER INSERT trigger</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#introduction-to-the-postgresql-after-insert-trigger" aria-label="Link to Introduction to the PostgreSQL AFTER INSERT trigger"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>In PostgreSQL, a trigger is a database object associated with a table, which is automatically fired in response to an <a class="" href="../postgresql-tutorial/postgresql-insert"><code>INSERT</code></a>, <a class="" href="../postgresql-tutorial/postgresql-update"><code>UPDATE</code></a>, <a class="" href="../postgresql-tutorial/postgresql-delete"><code>DELETE</code></a>, or <a class="" href="../postgresql-tutorial/postgresql-truncate-table"><code>TRUNCATE</code></a> event.</p>
<p>An <code>AFTER INSERT</code> trigger is a trigger that is fired after an <code>INSERT</code> event occurs on a table.</p>
<p>The <code>AFTER INSERT</code> trigger can access the newly inserted data using the <code>NEW</code> record variable. This <code>NEW</code> variable allows you to access the values of columns in the inserted row:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="sql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">NEW.column_name</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-[min(1rem,calc(50%-.8175rem))]" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>Typically, you use <code>AFTER INSERT</code> triggers for logging changes, updating related tables, or sending notifications based on the inserted data.</p>
<p>To create an <code>AFTER</code> <code>INSERT</code> trigger, you follow these steps:</p>
<p>First, <a class="" href="../postgresql-plpgsql/postgresql-create-function">define a function</a> that will execute when the trigger is activated:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="plsql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">CREATE OR REPLACE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> FUNCTION trigger_function()</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">   RETURNS </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">TRIGGER</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="3"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">   LANGUAGE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> PLPGSQL</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="4"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">AS</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="5"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">$$</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="6"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">BEGIN</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="7"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)">   -- trigger logic</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="8"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)">   -- ...</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="9"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">   RETURN</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> NEW;</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="10"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">END</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">;</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="11"><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">$$</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-4" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>The <code>RETURN NEW</code> statement indicates that the function returns the modified row, which is the <code>NEW</code> row.</p>
<p>Second, create an <code>AFTER</code> <code>INSERT</code> trigger and bind the function to it:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="sql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">CREATE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> TRIGGER</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)"> trigger_name</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">AFTER</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> INSERT</span></span>
